{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NKLESTBq4Sq1nWVaoFn2hD","type":"tool_result","content":"95\t\n96\tdef item_ledger(root: Path, m: dict[str, Any], item_id: str, merges: list[dict[str, Any]] | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n97\t    \"\"\"{\"item\", \"rows\", \"summary\"}: one row per act between item_id's first\n98\t    spec commit and its merge (merge_introducing_records, the same\n99\t    derivation doctor's proof two and attest both already read) or HEAD\n100\t    when the item has not merged yet.\n101\t\n102\t    merges, when given, is _merges_reachable's own result -- cmd_ledger\n103\t    computes it once and passes it here for every item, rather than each\n104\t    item walking HEAD's merges again (issue #153).\n105\t\n106\t    Each commit gets exactly one class, in this order: the merge commit\n107\t    itself is \"merge\"; a commit authored by the executor identity\n108\t    (executor_identity) is \"change\"; a commit introducing an approval\n109\t    record is \"approve\", whoever committed it -- an operator's decision,\n110\t    however it reached git; a commit introducing a spec-gate, build, or\n111\t    verify record, authored by the driver identity (driver_identity) or\n112\t    the records app, is \"record\"; the same, authored by a person, is\n113\t    \"launch\" for build or verify (spec-gate records the app always\n114\t    commits, in every template this product ships) -- unless that\n115\t    record's own product_version predates v0.18.0, when driver_identity\n116\t    did not yet exist to tell the two apart, and the row is\n117\t    \"record-or-launch\" with a note, counted in neither summary total\n118\t    rather than guessed; a person's commit touching the spec is \"spec\"\n119\t    before the first approval record and \"amend\" after; anything else by\n120\t    a person is \"transport\" (a merge of main among them).\"\"\"\n121\t    specs_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"specs\"]\n122\t    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n123\t    specs_prefix = f\"{specs_rel.rstrip('/')}/{item_id}/\"\n124\t    records_prefix = f\"{records_rel.rstrip('/')}/{item_id}/\"\n125\t    empty_summary = {\"operator_acts\": 0, \"product_acts\": 0, \"executor_commits\": 0,\n126\t                     \"stops\": 0, \"since\": None}\n127\t\n128\t    first_spec_sha = first_commit_touching(root, str(Path(specs_rel) / item_id))\n129\t    if first_spec_sha is None:\n130\t        return {\"item\": item_id, \"rows\": [], \"summary\": empty_summary}\n131\t\n132\t    if merges is None:\n133\t        merges, refusal = _merges_reachable(root)\n134\t        if refusal:\n135\t            return {\"item\": item_id, \"rows\": [], \"summary\": empty_summary}\n136\t    merge_sha, _ = merge_introducing_records(root, records_rel, item_id, STAGES, merges=merges)\n137\t    if merge_sha is not None:\n138\t        branch_tip = next(mrg[\"parents\"][1] for mrg in merges if mrg[\"sha\"] == merge_sha)\n139\t        commits = commits_with_diffs(root, f\"{first_spec_sha}^\", end=branch_tip)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f72eeed-ce9e-4916-937c-8eb7f16a3662","uuid":"06ef53e4-4537-4988-bd14-5c6a64ae8341","timestamp":"2026-10-07T20:54:53.714Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-349/attavo/ledger.py","content":"\ndef item_ledger(root: Path, m: dict[str, Any], item_id: str, merges: list[dict[str, Any]] | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"{\"item\", \"rows\", \"summary\"}: one row per act between item_id's first\n    spec commit and its merge (merge_introducing_records, the same\n    derivation doctor's proof two and attest both already read) or HEAD\n    when the item has not merged yet.\n\n    merges, when given, is _merges_reachable's own result -- cmd_ledger\n    computes it once and passes it here for every item, rather than each\n    item walking HEAD's merges again (issue #153).\n\n    Each commit gets exactly one class, in this order: the merge commit\n    itself is \"merge\"; a commit authored by the executor identity\n    (executor_identity) is \"change\"; a commit introducing an approval\n    record is \"approve\", whoever committed it -- an operator's decision,\n    however it reached git; a commit introducing a spec-gate, build, or\n    verify record, authored by the driver identity (driver_identity) or\n    the records app, is \"record\"; the same, authored by a person, is\n    \"launch\" for build or verify (spec-gate records the app always\n    commits, in every template this product ships) -- unless that\n    record's own product_version predates v0.18.0, when driver_identity\n    did not yet exist to tell the two apart, and the row is\n    \"record-or-launch\" with a note, counted in neither summary total\n    rather than guessed; a person's commit touching the spec is \"spec\"\n    before the first approval record and \"amend\" after; anything else by\n    a person is \"transport\" (a merge of main among them).\"\"\"\n    specs_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"specs\"]\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n    specs_prefix = f\"{specs_rel.rstrip('/')}/{item_id}/\"\n    records_prefix = f\"{records_rel.rstrip('/')}/{item_id}/\"\n    empty_summary = {\"operator_acts\": 0, \"product_acts\": 0, \"executor_commits\": 0,\n                     \"stops\": 0, \"since\": None}\n\n    first_spec_sha = first_commit_touching(root, str(Path(specs_rel) / item_id))\n    if first_spec_sha is None:\n        return {\"item\": item_id, \"rows\": [], \"summary\": empty_summary}\n\n    if merges is None:\n        merges, refusal = _merges_reachable(root)\n        if refusal:\n            return {\"item\": item_id, \"rows\": [], \"summary\": empty_summary}\n    merge_sha, _ = merge_introducing_records(root, records_rel, item_id, STAGES, merges=merges)\n    if merge_sha is not None:\n        branch_tip = next(mrg[\"parents\"][1] for mrg in merges if mrg[\"sha\"] == merge_sha)\n        commits = commits_with_diffs(root, f\"{first_spec_sha}^\", end=branch_tip)","numLines":45,"startLine":95,"totalLines":363}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NKLESTBq4Sq1nWVaoFn2hD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
